# Scoped verify freshness, end to end through the native verify-status action.
#
# Six sessions share this checkout, so the whole-tree fingerprint goes STALE
# within seconds of a PASS -- almost always for a file the asking session never
# wrote. The scoped `check PATH...` form is what lets a session hold evidence
# about its own file list. This test drives that form against a throwaway git
# repo and asserts both directions: my untouched path stays FRESH while a second
# writer edits an unrelated file, and every way of losing that evidence still
# reports STALE.
#
# Nothing here touches the real tmp/ze-verify.status or tmp/ze-verify-manifest.txt.
# The native action resolves both against the working directory, and every command
# below runs with the working directory inside the scratch repo it creates.
#
# If the scoped arm regressed to the whole-tree compare, `check mine.txt` would
# report STALE after the second writer's edit and seq=2 would fail.

option=timeout:value=60s




cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture runner/verify-scope-freshness-scoped
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=scratch-repo-ready
expect=stdout:contains=scoped-fresh-for-my-path
expect=stdout:contains=unscoped-still-whole-tree
expect=stdout:contains=scoped-stale-for-their-path
expect=stdout:contains=scoped-stale-for-my-own-edit
expect=stdout:contains=moved-path-stays-stale
expect=stdout:contains=red-run-stale-for-every-scope
